 # Voxel-Specific Shading Pipelines
-
-
 ## Overview
-Voxel-Specific Shading Pipelines compute illumination for data stored in discrete 3D voxel grids, handling both surface-like boundaries and volumetric density. They differ from continuous surface shading by operating on discrete voxel coordinates and neighbor-dependent lighting calculations [G], and include [Voxel Shading Pipeline](3898-voxel-shading-pipeline.md), [Fast Shading for Voxel Engines](5606-fast-shading-for-voxel-engines.md), [Voxel Shader Volumetric Ray Marching](16930-voxel-shader-volumetric-ray-marching.md), and [Voxmat Path Tracer](21082-voxmat-path-tracer.md).
-
+Voxel-Specific Shading Pipelines compute illumination for data stored in discrete 3D voxel grids, handling both surface-like boundaries and volumetric density [G]. They differ from continuous surface shading by operating on discrete voxel coordinates and neighbor-dependent lighting calculations [G], and include [Voxel Shading Pipeline](3898-voxel-shading-pipeline.md), [Fast Shading for Voxel Engines](5606-fast-shading-for-voxel-engines.md), [Voxel Shader Volumetric Ray Marching](16930-voxel-shader-volumetric-ray-marching.md), and [Voxmat Path Tracer](21082-voxmat-path-tracer.md).
 ## Shared principles
-All methods operate on a 3D voxel grid indexed by integer coordinates $(x, y, z)$ . Lighting calculations frequently depend on immediate neighboring voxels to determine occlusion or shading factors, rather than casting long-distance rays for every sample, except in explicit ray-marching variants . Inputs include block types, palette indices, or continuous scalar/vector fields stored in the voxel cells .
